change is a collectible the uppers still see, but that is no","+                // longer emitted (or aggregated) by this task.","+                for (&collectible, &count) in task.iter_pending_collectibles() {","+                    if count < 0","+                        && let Some((flag, _)) = collectibles.get_mut(&collectible)","+                    {","+                        *flag = true","+                    }","+                }"," ","                 let is_dirty = task.has_dirty();","                 let has_dirty_container = task.has_dirty_containers();","@@ -3949,6 +3986,12 @@ impl TurboTasksBackend {","                 }","                 drop(task);"," ","+                if let Err(message) =","+                    operation::check_pending_collectibles_invariant(&mut ctx, task_id)","+                {","+                    panic!(\"{message}\");","+                }","+","                 if should_be_in_upper {","                     for upper_id in uppers {","                         let upper = ctx.task(upper_id, TaskDataCategory::All);"],"additions":44,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"turbopack/crates/turbo-tasks-backend/src/backend/operation/aggregation_update.rs","lines":["@@ -148,6 +148,103 @@ pub fn is_root_node(aggregation_number: u32) -> bool {","     aggregation_number == u32::MAX"," }"," ","+/// Whether the task counts as dirty for strongly consistent reads, i.e. as a dirty container that","+/// is not clean in the current session in all of its uppers.","+fn is_effectively_dirty(task: &TaskGuard<'_>) -> bool {","+    task.is_dirty().is_some() || task.has_dirty_containers()","+}","+","+/// Delayed collectible propagation: decides which collectible changes of `update`, an update of","+/// the contribution of `task` to its uppers, are sent now. Must be called under the lock of `task`,","+/// after its dirty state has been updated, for every outgoing update of the task that changes","+/// collectibles or can make the task clean.","+///","+/// - While the task is dirty (itself or through its children), the collectible changes are moved","+///   into the task's `pending_collectibles`, where positive and negative changes of the same","+///   collectible cancel out. Only the dirty state part of `update` is sent. This also applies when","+///   the task has no uppers yet: a task that is executing can temporarily have many collectibles","+///   that it removes again before it's clean, and these shouldn't be propagated.","+/// - Once the task is clean, the pending changes are netted with the changes of `update` and added","+///   to it, so `update` stays normalized (one entry per collectible). The update that makes the","+///   task clean always passes here, so they are sent together with it. Without uppers, the update","+///   isn't sent, which drops the pending changes: nobody has seen the contribution.","+///","+/// A dirty subgraph often changes the same collectibles back and forth before it is clean again,","+/// e.g. a task that takes the collectibles of a recomputed child cancels the child's changes when","+/// it re-executes. Delaying the changes avoids propagating them through all uppers twice.","+///","+/// This keeps the invariant that a task with pending collectibles is a dirty container (not clean","+/// in the current session) in all its uppers, so these uppers aren't clean either. A strongly","+/// consistent read waits until the task it reads is clean, so it never misses pending changes.","+/// Collectibles are only stable after a strongly consistent read of their source: a read that","+/// isn't strongly consistent may miss changes that are still pending in the dirty subgraph.","+///","+/// [`AggregatedDataUpdate::from_task`] subtracts the pending changes, so that new and removed","+/// uppers see the same contribution as the existing uppers.","+pub fn stage_outgoing_collectibles(task: &mut TaskGuard<'_>, update: &mut AggregatedDataUpdate) {","+    let has_pending = !task.is_pending_collectibles_empty();","+    if update.collectibles_update.is_empty() && !has_pending {","+        return;","+    }","+    let is_dirty = is_effectively_dirty(task);","+    if !is_dirty && !has_pending {","+        // Clean and nothing pending: send the changes as they are.","+        return;","+    }","+    for (collectible, count) in take(&mut update.collectibles_update) {","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible, count);","+    }","+    if !is_dirty && let Some(pending) = task.take_pending_collectibles() {","+        update.collectibles_update.extend(pending);","+    }","+}","+","+/// Checks the invariant of delayed collectible propagation for `task_id` (see","+/// [`stage_outgoing_collectibles`]): a task with pending collectibles is effectively dirty and is","+/// listed as an effectively dirty container (dirty, not clean in the current session) in every","+/// upper. Used by `verify_aggregation_graph`, which runs while the graph is idle.","+#[cfg(any(test, feature = \"verify_aggregation_graph\"))]","+pub fn check_pending_collectibles_invariant(","+    ctx: &mut ExecuteContext<'_>,","+    task_id: TaskId,","+) -> Result<(), String> {","+    let (pending, is_dirty, upper_ids) = {","+        let task = ctx.task(task_id, TaskDataCategory::Meta);","+        if task.is_pending_collectibles_empty() {","+            return Ok(());","+        }","+        (","+            task.pending_collectibles_len(),","+            is_effectively_dirty(&task),","+            get_uppers(&task),","+        )","+    };","+    if !is_dirty {","+        return Err(format!(","+            \"Task {task_id} has {pending} pending collectibles, but is not dirty\"","+        ));","+    }","+    for upper_id in upper_ids {","+        let upper = ctx.task(upper_id, TaskDataCategory::Meta);","+        let dirty = upper","+            .get_aggregated_dirty_containers(&task_id)","+            .copied()","+            .unwrap_or_default();","+        let clean = upper","+            .get_aggregated_current_session_clean_containers(&task_id)","+            .copied()","+            .unwrap_or_default();","+        if dirty <= 0 || dirty <= clean {","+            return Err(format!(","+                \"Task {task_id} has {pending} pending collectibles, but is not a dirty container \\","+                 of its upper {upper_id} (dirty count {dirty}, current session clean count \\","+                 {clean})\"","+            ));","+        }","+    }","+    Ok(())","+}","+"," /// Returns a list of tasks that are considered as \"following\" the task."," fn get_followers_with_aggregation_number(","     task: &TaskGuard<'_>,","@@ -451,10 +548,16 @@ impl AggregationUpdateJob {","         )","     }"," ","+    /// Creates a job that sends `update` to the uppers of `task`. Callers that send collectible","+    /// changes or can make the task clean must pass `update` through","+    /// [`stage_outgoing_collectibles`] first.","     pub fn data_update(","         task: &mut TaskGuard<'_>,","         update: AggregatedDataUpdate,","     ) -> Option<AggregationUpdateJob> {","+        if update.is_empty() {","+            return None;","+        }","         let upper_ids: SmallVec<_> = get_uppers(task);","         if !upper_ids.is_empty() {","             Some(","@@ -516,7 +619,9 @@ impl AggregatedDataUpdate {","         let aggregation = get_aggregation_number(task);","         let mut dirty_count = 0;","         let mut current_session_clean_count = 0;","-        let collectibles_update = if is_aggregating_node(aggregation) {","+        // Whether `collectibles_update` can contain more than one entry per collectible.","+        let mut need_optimize = false;","+        let mut collectibles_update = if is_aggregating_node(aggregation) {","             dirty_count = task","                 .get_aggregated_dirty_container_count()","                 .copied()","@@ -536,10 +641,19 @@ impl AggregatedDataUpdate {","                     collectibles_update.push((*collectible, 1));","                 }","             }","+            // A collectible can be listed twice: own and aggregated.","+            need_optimize =","+                !task.is_collectibles_empty() && !task.is_aggregated_collectibles_empty();","             collectibles_update","         } else {","             task.iter_collectibles().map(|(&k, &v)| (k, v)).collect()","         };","+        // The uppers haven't seen the pending changes yet (see `stage_outgoing_collectibles`), so","+        // subtract them.","+        if !task.is_pending_collectibles_empty() {","+            collectibles_update.extend(task.iter_pending_collectibles().map(|(&k, &v)| (k, -v)));","+            need_optimize = true;","+        }","         let (dirty, current_session_clean) = task.dirty_state();","         if dirty {","             dirty_count += 1;","@@ -549,6 +663,12 @@ impl AggregatedDataUpdate {","         }"," ","         let mut result = Self::new().collectibles_update(collectibles_update);","+        // Duplicate entries must net out before the update is applied: otherwise a collectible","+        // could disappear and appear again in the upper, which invalidates its readers. Not all","+        // callers optimize the update (`balance_edge` applies it while holding both locks).","+        if need_optimize {","+            result = result.optimize();","+        }","         if dirty_count > 0 {","             result = result.dirty_container_update(","                 task.id(),","@@ -862,6 +982,7 @@ impl AggregatedDataUpdate {","                 result.collectibles_update.push((*collectible, -1));","             }","         }","+        stage_outgoing_collectibles(task, &mut result);","         result","     }"," ","@@ -5536,6 +5657,363 @@ mod follower_debt_tests {","     }"," }"," ","+/// Deterministic tests of delayed collectible propagation (see `stage_outgoing_collectibles`).","+#[cfg(test)]","+mod delayed_collectibles_tests {","+    use smallvec::smallvec;","+    use turbo_tasks::{TaskPriority, TurboTasks};","+","+    use super::{","+        AggregatedDataUpdate, AggregationUpdateQueue, check_pending_collectibles_invariant,","+        follower_debt_tests::{","+            FOLLOWER, INNER, UPPER, add, aggregated, balance, collectible, id, remove, run,","+            setup_with_data, uppers,","+        },","+        stage_outgoing_collectibles,","+    };","+    use crate::{","+        backend::{","+            TaskDataCategory, TurboTasksBackend,","+            operation::{ExecuteContext, UpdateCollectibleOperation},","+            storage_schema::TaskStorageAccessors,","+        },","+        data::{AggregationNumber, CellRef, CollectibleRef, Dirtyness},","+    };","+","+    fn set_dirty(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32, dirty: bool) {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let job = {","+            let mut task = ctx.task(id(task), TaskDataCategory::All);","+            task.update_dirty_state(dirty.then_some(Dirtyness::Dirty {","+                parent_priority: TaskPriority::leaf(),","+                #[cfg(feature = \"task_dirty_cause\")]","+                cause: turbo_tasks::TaskDirtyCause::InitialDirty,","+            }))","+        };","+        if let Some(job) = job {","+            let mut queue = AggregationUpdateQueue::new_without_optimizations();","+            queue.push(job);","+            queue.execute(&mut ctx);","+        }","+    }","+","+    fn emit(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32, count: i32) {","+        UpdateCollectibleOperation::run(id(task), collectible(), count, ExecuteContext::new(tt));","+    }","+","+    fn pending(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32) -> i32 {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let task = ctx.task(id(task), TaskDataCategory::Meta);","+        task.get_pending_collectibles(&collectible())","+            .copied()","+            .unwrap_or_default()","+    }","+","+    fn has_dirty_containers(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32) -> bool {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let task = ctx.task(id(task), TaskDataCategory::Meta);","+        task.has_dirty_containers()","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn changes_net_while_dirty_and_flush_with_clean() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        assert!(has_dirty_containers(&tt, 1));","+","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (0, 1));","+        emit(&tt, 2, -1);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (0, 0));","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (0, 1));","+","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert!(!has_dirty_containers(&tt, 1));","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (1, 0));","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn edges_use_the_published_contribution() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER), (3, UPPER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+","+        run(&tt, [add(3, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), aggregated(&tt, 3)), (0, 0));","+","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), aggregated(&tt, 3)), (1, 1));","+","+        run(&tt, [remove(3, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), aggregated(&tt, 3)), (1, 0));","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn dirty_children_delay_changes_until_clean() {","+        // 3 is dirty, which makes 2 a task with a dirty container, while 2 itself is clean.","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER + 1), (2, UPPER), (3, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2), add(2, 3)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 3, true);","+        assert!(has_dirty_containers(&tt, 2));","+","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (0, 1));","+","+        // The child becoming clean makes 2 clean, which sends the pending changes.","+        set_dirty(&tt, 3, false);","+        assert!(!has_dirty_containers(&tt, 1));","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (1, 0));","+    }","+","+    /// A task that read the collectibles of an upper, so it is invalidated when they change.","+    const READER: u32 = 999;","+","+    /// Registers `READER` as a dependent of the collectibles of `upper`.","+    fn add_reader(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, upper: u32) {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let mut task = ctx.task(id(upper), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        let _ = task.add_collectibles_dependents((collectible().collectible_type, id(READER)));","+    }","+","+    /// Whether `READER` was invalidated.","+    fn reader_is_dirty(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>) -> bool {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let task = ctx.task(id(READER), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        task.get_dirty().is_some()","+    }","+","+    fn set_aggregation_number(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32, number: u32) {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        let mut task = ctx.task(id(task), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        task.set_aggregation_number(AggregationNumber {","+            base: number,","+            distance: 0,","+            effective: number,","+        });","+    }","+","+    /// A task that becomes an inner task of a new upper while it has pending changes contributes","+    /// only its published collectibles. Its own collectibles and the subtracted pending changes","+    /// must net out before they are applied, so the new upper never sees the unpublished","+    /// collectible appear and disappear again, which would invalidate its readers.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn new_inner_edge_nets_out_pending_changes() {","+        // 2 is a follower of 1, and an inner task of 3, so changes of 2 are staged for 3.","+        let tt = setup_with_data(","+            &[(1, UPPER), (2, FOLLOWER), (3, FOLLOWER + 1), (READER, 0)],","+            false,","+        );","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2), add(3, 2)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!(pending(&tt, 2), 1);","+        add_reader(&tt, 1);","+","+        // Lowering the aggregation number of 2 turns the follower edge into an inner edge.","+        set_aggregation_number(&tt, 2, INNER);","+        run(&tt, [balance(1, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!(uppers(&tt, 2), vec![(id(1), 1), (id(3), 1)]);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), aggregated(&tt, 3)), (0, 0));","+        assert!(","+            !reader_is_dirty(&tt),","+            \"the unpublished collectible must not invalidate the reader\"","+        );","+","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), aggregated(&tt, 3)), (1, 1));","+        assert!(reader_is_dirty(&tt), \"publishing invalidates the reader\");","+    }","+","+    /// A dirty task without uppers delays its changes too: an executing task can temporarily have","+    /// collectibles that it removes again before it's clean.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn changes_without_uppers_are_delayed_until_clean() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!(pending(&tt, 2), 1);","+","+        // A new upper sees only the published contribution.","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (0, 1));","+","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert_eq!((aggregated(&tt, 1), pending(&tt, 2)), (1, 0));","+    }","+","+    /// Without uppers, becoming clean drops the pending changes: nobody has seen them.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn clean_without_uppers_drops_pending_changes() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!(pending(&tt, 2), 1);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert_eq!(pending(&tt, 2), 0);","+","+        // The collectible is still part of the contribution of 2.","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!(aggregated(&tt, 1), 1);","+    }","+","+    /// `from_task` subtracts each pending count once, even when an aggregating task lists a","+    /// collectible twice (own and aggregated), and adds pending removals.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn from_task_nets_pending_changes() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(2, UPPER)], false);","+        let other = other_collectible();","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+        let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        let _ = task.update_collectibles_positive_crossing(collectible(), 1);","+        task.update_aggregated_collectibles(collectible(), |_| Some(1));","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 1);","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(other, -1);","+        let mut update = AggregatedDataUpdate::from_task(&mut task).collectibles_update;","+        update.sort_by_key(|(collectible, _)| collectible.cell.task);","+        assert_eq!(update.as_slice(), [(collectible(), 1), (other, 1)]);","+    }","+","+    /// When both the own and the aggregated entry of a collectible are pending, `from_task` must","+    /// not leave opposite entries for it.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn from_task_combines_own_and_aggregated_entries() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(2, UPPER)], false);","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+        let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        let _ = task.update_collectibles_positive_crossing(collectible(), 1);","+        task.update_aggregated_collectibles(collectible(), |_| Some(1));","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 2);","+        let update = AggregatedDataUpdate::from_task(&mut task).collectibles_update;","+        assert!(update.is_empty(), \"{update:?}\");","+    }","+","+    /// Edge balancing of an aggregating task whose own and aggregated entries are both pending","+    /// doesn't invalidate the readers of the new upper, which already sees the collectible from","+    /// another inner task.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn new_inner_edge_with_own_and_aggregated_pending_changes() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(","+            &[(1, UPPER), (2, FOLLOWER), (3, FOLLOWER + 1), (READER, 0)],","+            false,","+        );","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2), add(3, 2)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        {","+            let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+            let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::All);","+            let _ = task.update_collectibles_positive_crossing(collectible(), 1);","+            task.update_aggregated_collectibles(collectible(), |_| Some(1));","+            let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 2);","+        }","+        {","+            // Another inner task of 1 contributes the collectible already.","+            let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+            let mut task = ctx.task(id(1), TaskDataCategory::All);","+            task.update_aggregated_collectibles(collectible(), |_| Some(1));","+        }","+        add_reader(&tt, 1);","+","+        // Still aggregating, but lower than 1, so the follower edge becomes an inner edge.","+        set_aggregation_number(&tt, 2, UPPER / 2);","+        run(&tt, [balance(1, 2)]);","+        assert_eq!(uppers(&tt, 2), vec![(id(1), 1), (id(3), 1)]);","+        assert_eq!(aggregated(&tt, 1), 1);","+        assert!(","+            !reader_is_dirty(&tt),","+            \"the unpublished collectible must not invalidate the reader\"","+        );","+    }","+","+    /// A clean flush nets the update's changes with the pending ones: one non-zero entry per","+    /// collectible.","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn clean_flush_combines_update_and_pending_changes() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        let other = other_collectible();","+        let third = CollectibleRef {","+            cell: CellRef {","+                task: id(1002),","+                ..collectible().cell","+            },","+            ..collectible()","+        };","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+        let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::All);","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 1);","+        let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(other, 1);","+        let mut update = AggregatedDataUpdate::new()","+            .collectibles_update(smallvec![(collectible(), -1), (third, 1)]);","+        stage_outgoing_collectibles(&mut task, &mut update);","+        let mut update = update.collectibles_update;","+        update.sort_by_key(|(collectible, _)| collectible.cell.task);","+        assert_eq!(update.as_slice(), [(other, 1), (third, 1)]);","+        assert!(task.is_pending_collectibles_empty());","+    }","+","+    fn other_collectible() -> CollectibleRef {","+        CollectibleRef {","+            cell: CellRef {","+                task: id(1001),","+                ..collectible().cell","+            },","+            ..collectible()","+        }","+    }","+","+    fn check(tt: &TurboTasks<TurboTasksBackend>, task: u32) -> Result<(), String> {","+        let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(tt);","+        check_pending_collectibles_invariant(&mut ctx, id(task))","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn invariant_check_accepts_pending_changes_of_dirty_tasks() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, true);","+        emit(&tt, 2, 1);","+        assert_eq!(pending(&tt, 2), 1);","+        assert_eq!(check(&tt, 2), Ok(()));","+        set_dirty(&tt, 2, false);","+        assert_eq!(check(&tt, 2), Ok(()));","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn invariant_check_reports_pending_changes_of_clean_tasks() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        {","+            let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+            let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::Meta);","+            let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 1);","+        }","+        let error = check(&tt, 2).unwrap_err();","+        assert!(error.contains(\"is not dirty\"), \"{error}\");","+    }","+","+    #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\")]","+    async fn invariant_check_reports_pending_changes_missing_in_upper() {","+        let tt = setup_with_data(&[(1, UPPER), (2, INNER)], false);","+        run(&tt, [add(1, 2)]);","+        {","+            // Dirty and pending, but the dirty state was never sent to the upper.","+            let mut ctx = ExecuteContext::new(&tt);","+            let mut task = ctx.task(id(2), TaskDataCategory::All);","+            task.set_dirty(Dirtyness::Dirty {","+                parent_priority: TaskPriority::leaf(),","+                #[cfg(feature = \"task_dirty_cause\")]","+                cause: turbo_tasks::TaskDirtyCause::InitialDirty,","+            });","+            let _ = task.update_pending_collectibles_count(collectible(), 1);","+        }","+        let error = check(&tt, 2).unwrap_err();","+        assert!(error.contains(\"not a dirty container\"), \"{error}\");","+    }","+}","+"," /// Deterministic tests of the deferred removal queue: within one queue, edge removals are"," /// processed after additions and balancing."," #[cfg(test)]"],"additions":479,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"turbopack/crates/turbo-tasks-backend/src/backend/operation/cleanup_old_edges.rs","lines":["@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ use crate::{","                 AggregationUpdateJob, AggregationUpdateQueue, InnerOfUppersLostFollowersJob,","                 get_aggregation_number, get_uppers, is_aggregating_node,","             },","+            stage_outgoing_collectibles,","         },","         storage_schema::{ActivenessAccessors, TaskStorageAccessors},","     },","@@ -256,10 +257,9 @@ fn cleanup_old_edges_inner(","                         collectible_type: ty,","                     });","                 }","-                queue.extend(AggregationUpdateJob::data_update(","-                    &mut task,","-                    AggregatedDataUpdate::new().collectibles_update(collectibles),","-                ));","+                let mut update = AggregatedDataUpdate::new().collectibles_update(collectibles);","+                stage_outgoing_collectibles(&mut task, &mut update);","+                queue.extend(AggregationUpdateJob::data_update(&mut task, update));"],"additions":4,"deletions":4,"truncated":false}],"additions":533,"deletions":9,"truncated":true,"file_count":5},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-17T18:43:25.123823+00:00"}